import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Privacy — Potpuri" bare>
  <main>
    <a class="back" href="/">← Potpuri</a>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated October 2026</p>

    <p class="draft">A working draft. Have a lawyer review this before launch.</p>

    <h2>What we hold</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account:</strong> email, handle, display name, date of birth, time zone.</li>
      <li><strong>Reading:</strong> which pages you have read and when, your position in each book, your streak.</li>
      <li><strong>Your marks:</strong> likes, highlights, and personal book ratings.</li>
      <li><strong>Reading companion:</strong> monthly request counts and the time of your last request, to enforce usage limits. We do not store personal phrases or their explanation answers. Card translations are stored by public book card and language, and may be reused by other paid readers.</li>
      <li><strong>Subscription:</strong> Stripe customer/subscription identifiers, renewal/end date, membership state, and founding-offer reservations. Card/payment details are handled by Stripe, not stored by Potpuri.</li>
      <li><strong>Social:</strong> friendships, and requests you have sent or received.</li>
      <li><strong>Technical:</strong> session records with approximate IP and browser, kept for security.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Why we hold it</h2>
    <p>To run the service you asked for: remembering your place, counting your daily pages,
    keeping your streak, and showing friends what you are reading when you allow it. The legal
    basis is performance of our contract with you. Security logging rests on our legitimate
    interest in keeping accounts safe.</p>

    <h2>Date of birth</h2>
    <p>We ask for it to confirm you are old enough to use Potpuri, and we keep it so we do not
    have to ask again. It is not shown to anyone else.</p>

    <h2>What we do not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No advertising, and no sale of your data.</li>
      <li>No third-party analytics on what you read.</li>
      <li>No profiling of minors.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>What a person reads can reveal a great deal about them. We treat reading history as
    sensitive even where the law does not require it.</p>

    <h2>Who can see your reading</h2>
    <p>Your profile is visible to friends by default. You can set it to public or to only you,
    and you can hide an individual book from your profile at any time.</p>

    <h2>Optional AI explanations and translations</h2>
    <p>When you submit a phrase to Puri, we send that phrase,
    your chosen answer language, and explanation or translation instructions to OpenRouter
    and Google Gemini. When you request a card translation, we send only the current card text
    and the chosen language, then store its translation for reuse. We do not send your account details, reading history, or the whole
    book. Do not submit sensitive information. We request providers that disallow data
    collection and support zero data retention; provider billing and operational metadata
    may still be processed under their own policies.</p>
    <p><a href="https://openrouter.ai/privacy">OpenRouter privacy policy</a> ·
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google privacy policy</a> ·
    <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy">Stripe privacy policy</a>.
    AI answers may be inaccurate; using the companion is optional.</p>

    <h2>Bring your own API key (BYOK)</h2>
    <p>Free BYOK supports OpenAI, Anthropic and OpenRouter. Your browser sends your selected
    text, chosen language, model and API key directly to the selected provider over HTTPS.
    The provider also receives your IP address. Your own API account is billed; consumer
    ChatGPT/Codex subscriptions are not API credits. We do not receive or store the key,
    prompt or BYOK answer. We keep only an account-level monthly reservation count for
    the 50-request app allowance. Reservations count even if a provider request fails or is cancelled.</p>
    <p>Keys and BYOK translations are held only in page memory and disappear on reload or
    navigation. No encrypted vault, sync or key recovery is provided. Browser scripts,
    extensions or a compromised device could still access an active key. Use a dedicated,
    revocable key with a low provider-side spending limit. The app allowance is not a
    security boundary or a spending cap. No automatic fallback to paid membership inference occurs.</p>
    <p>Direct providers have their own retention and privacy policies. For OpenRouter BYOK
    we request zero-data-retention routing and deny data collection; this may limit model
    availability. Those routing controls do not apply to direct OpenAI or Anthropic requests.
    <a href="https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy/">OpenAI privacy</a> ·
    <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy">Anthropic privacy</a> ·
    <a href="https://openrouter.ai/privacy">OpenRouter privacy</a>.</p>

    <h2>How we protect it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Passwords are hashed with Argon2id and are never recoverable.</li>
      <li>Two-factor secrets are encrypted before they are stored.</li>
      <li>Session cookies are HttpOnly, and only a hash of each session is stored.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can access, correct, export or delete your data. Email
    <a href="mailto:privacy@bookworm.example">privacy@bookworm.example</a> and we will respond
    within one month. You may also complain to your local data protection authority.</p>

    <h2>Keeping</h2>
    <p>We keep your data while your account is open. Closing your account removes your personal
    data; anonymous aggregate counts, such as how many people liked a page, may remain.</p>

    <nav class="links">
      <a href="/legal/terms">Terms</a>
      <a href="/legal/takedown">Report a work</a>
    </nav>
  </main>
</Base>

